    "title": "Transitive Closure of a Directed Graph",
    "category": "Graphs",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "Given a directed graph with N vertices, determine whether every vertex is reachable from every other vertex. Output the complete reachability matrix.",
    "input": "\u2022 First line contains integers N and M. \u2022 Next M lines contain directed edges.",
    "output": "Print an N \u00d7 N matrix where the value at row i and column j is 1 if vertex j is reachable from i, otherwise 0.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 1 \u2264 N \u2264 500 \u2022 0 \u2264 M \u2264 N(N\u22121)"
